>1999</year><article-title>Control strategies for human intestinal nematode infections.</article-title><source>Adv Parasitol</source><volume>42</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10050275</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000399-Candolfi1"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Candolfi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Remington</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Mitogen- and antigen-specific proliferation of T cells in murine toxoplasmosis is inhibited by reactive nitrogen intermediates.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>1995</fpage><lpage>2001</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8168967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000399-Dai1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dai</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gottstein</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Nitric oxide-mediated immunosuppression following murine Echinococcus multilocularis infection.</article-title><source>Immunology</source><volume>97</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10447721</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000399-Geiger1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Geiger</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Caldas</surname><given-names>IR</given-names></name><name><surname>Mc Glone</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Campi-Azevedo</surname><given-names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>De Oliveira</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Stage-sp